  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Enhanced Air Traffic Control A.S. Degree - Local GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published July 31, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7803/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: SCC Local (L1A/L1B, L2, L3, L4, L5, L6, L7A/L7B); the map labels Ethnic Studies 'Cal-GETC Area 6' even on this Local GE pattern — transcribed as an Ethnic Studies core slot. Official Total Units: 60-61; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 13 + 15 + 4 + 12 + 12 + 4 = 60 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page). Semester sums verified against the map's 13-14 / 15 / 4 / 12 / 12 / 4 headers. This seed models the Tower Cohort path (first-listed options); the En Route Cohort substitutes ATC 320-323 for 310-313 and ATC 325 for 315. Choice slots: (1) GE ENGL C1000 / * 488 / H+ ESLW 340, L1A — ENGL C1000 selected; (2) GE INDIS 313 / HCD 310 Life Development Skills (3), L7B — INDIS 313 selected; (3) ATC 310 / 320 Terminal 1/En Route 1 (3) — ATC 310 selected; (4) ATC 311 / 321 (3) — ATC 311 selected; (5) ATC 312 / 322 (3) — ATC 312 selected; (6) ATC 313 / 323 (3) — ATC 313 selected; (7) ATC 315 / 325 Simulation Training (4) — ATC 315 selected. In-plan prereqs (Tower path): ATC 300 requires ATC 200; ATC 301 requires ATC 300; ATC 302 requires ATC 301; ATC 303 requires ATC 302; ATC 310 requires ATC 300, 301, 302, and 303; ATC 311 requires ATC 310; ATC 312 requires ATC 311; ATC 313 requires ATC 312; ATC 315 requires ATC 313 — all with grades of 'C' or better. En Route path prereqs documented (not in-plan): ATC 320 requires 300-303; ATC 321 requires 320; ATC 322 requires 321; ATC 323 requires 322; ATC 325 requires 323. Documented: students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 or Los Rios assessment placement; students not placing directly in STAT C1000 take the STAT 10/STAT C1000 combo. Documented FAA enrollment eligibility: English proficiency (ICAO Level 4 / AC60-28); under 31 by tentative job offer for FAA direct hire (nonFAA contract facilities exempt); minimum one year general work experience, one year full-time college, or equivalent; Federal Security Clearance; Class 3 Airman Medical to enter, FAA-endorsed medical/drug/psych exams at graduation; qualifying ATSA score for FAA direct-hire consideration. AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, SCC local GE Areas L1A/L1B, L2-L6, L7A/L7B. Electives: any courses numbered 100-499. Air Traffic Control, Business & Industry Meta Majors. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
